 comprehension on [this](https://github.com/pydata/pandas/blob/master/pandas/core/strings.py#L711) line. When the tuple is of length 1, it separates out the _string_ into individual chars, rather than iterating over the (single) tuple value(s).\n\n```\n>>> [x for x in ('ab', 'xy')]\n['ab', 'xy']\n>>> [x for x in ('ab')]\n['a', 'b']\n```\n\nI suppose code can be added beforehand to check for this particular case (though checking the length has the same issue - both examples above are length 2), but is there a cleaner fix?\n\nChecking the total number of groups in the regex match might be an alternative. \n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/comments/224360273/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"GeraintDuck","id":2274099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNzQwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2274099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraintDuck","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraintDuck/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/comments/224361770","html_url":"https://github.com/pandas-dev